      "notes": "Pharmacokinetic parameters after single IV and oral voriconazole, with and without tofacitinib\nS08 | DOI 10.3390/pharmaceutics13050740 | Table 2 (Lee et al. 2021; read from the PDF)\nMale Sprague-Dawley rats, about 7 weeks, 230-240 g at purchase (table gives body weight at study). IV 10 mg/kg over 1 min via the jugular vein (4 mL/kg; 0.9% NaCl containing 50% PEG 400); oral 20 mg/kg by gastric gavage (6 mL/kg). Carotid-artery plasma; HPLC with fluorescence detection; LLOQ not stated in the text read.\nIV sampling 0, 1, 5, 15, 30, 60, 120, 180, 240, 360, 480, 600 and/or 720 min; oral 0-960 min. Urine 0-24 h and whole GI tract at 24 h. Concentration curves are in Fig. 3 only (not digitized). \"Values are means ± standard deviation (SD).\"\n\"With TFC\" columns are a drug-interaction condition (tofacitinib 10 mg/kg IV or 20 mg/kg oral given together), not voriconazole alone. IV with-TFC n is 6 in the methods and 5 in the table. Footnote: \"* Significantly different from respective control group (p < 0.05).\"\nText: Vss with tofacitinib \"significantly greater (127%)\", but the table shows no asterisk on Vss. F is AUC oral / AUC IV per the methods; printed values 106 and 122.",
